2. PURPOSE

The purpose of this procedure is to perform the Global Control Process (GCP) review for Belgium tax reclaim cases maintained within STAR.

The control ensures reclaim statuses remain accurate, aged cases are identified and escalated, processing backlogs are monitored, and all relevant stakeholders provide timely updates to support effective reclaim processing and reporting.

The control is performed twice per year and includes:

* Population extraction
* Population reconciliation
* Status review
* Follow-up management
* Validation
* Control closure

Control Methodology

The GCP control utilizes two separate STAR reports.

The Primary Reclaim Population Report serves as the source population and contains all reclaim records within scope, including records without linked payment lines or beneficiary references.

The Detailed Tax Form User Report provides additional reclaim information such as beneficiary details, event details and address information.

As the Detailed Tax Form User Report may not contain all records present within the Primary Reclaim Population Report, a reconciliation must be performed before any status review activities commence.

